    source: MIM curation (#321)
    notes: molecular_formula '3Cl.Cr' -> '3Cl.Cr.6H2O'. The recorded value described the anhydrous salt
      while the label names a hydrate, understating the mass by 18 g/mol per water. Corrected because
      the label states 6 water(s) of hydration, and the recorded formula was byte-identical to the anhydrous
      parent CHEBI:53351's ChEBI formula ('3Cl.Cr') — the mark of a value inherited from the parent rather
      than measured for this record. Water appended in ChEBI's own dot-separated notation.
  - evidence_type: DATABASE_MATCH
    source: MIM curation (#374/#334)
    notes: 'Promoted from CHEBI:53351 (''chromium(3+) trichloride'') to the specific hydrate term CHEBI:53442
      (''chromium(3+) trichloride hexahydrate'') — MAPPING_SEMANTICS §3 step 1: the label names a hydrate,
      ChEBI has the term, so nothing needs minting and no closeMatch question arises. The previous term
      carried no water while the label states it. Found by cross-checking CultureBotAI/CultureMech#272
      (#374/#334).'
